<div class="content-header">
<h1 class="accent">
AWB Security Policy</h1>
</div>
<div class="padding-default padding-default-sides ">
<p>
AWB is committed to protecting information received from AWB website users and all transaction instructions between AWB and AWB website users.&nbsp; Please refer to the "<a href="/privacy" target="_blank" cmimpressionsent="1"><u><font color="#0066cc">AWB Internet Privacy Policy</font></u></a>" which is available on AWB's website, for details on how we manage personal information we collect through your use of the AWB website.</p>
<p>
&nbsp;</p>
<h4>
AWB Login Control</h4>
<p>
The AWB Login control is a secure application under 128-bit SSL key Encryption.&nbsp; All communication from your computer to our secure systems is encrypted to ensure the confidentiality of all data sent and received.</p>
<h4>
<br>
What is 128-bit SSL Encryption?</h4>
<p>
SSL is the industry standard protocol that protects the confidentiality, integrity and authenticity of data transferred during a session.</p>
<p>
Our website supports 128 Bit encryption of&nbsp;defined&nbsp;transactions that are made in secure areas of the Website using secure socket layers (SSL) technology.&nbsp;This means that these transactions can only be intercepted in their encrypted form.&nbsp;<br>
<br>
SSL encrypted pages are identifiable by "https" URLs and a padlock which appears in the bottom right hand corner of the browser status bar. Clicking on the padlock will allow you to view details of our SSL certificate.</p>
<p>
&nbsp;</p>
<p>
<img src='/image/1432086655445/security-certificate.jpg' alt="Security Certificate" class='    ' title="Security Certificate" />
</p>
<h4>
Using Internet Explorer – How to confirm an SSL connection</h4>
<p>
To confirm the AWB Login control is under SSL connection before logging in;</p>
<ol>
<li>
Right mouse click in the blue AWB Login area</li>
<li>
Select properties from the drop down menu</li>
</ol>
<p>
The properties window will appear confirming the AWB login control is under SSL connection.</p>
<p>
&nbsp;</p>
<p>
<img src='/image/1432086655201/awb-login-properties.jpg' alt="AWB Login properties" class='    ' title="AWB Login properties" />
</p>
<h4>
Using Firefox – How to confirm an SSL Connection</h4>
<p>
To confirm the AWB Login control is under SSL connection before logging in;</p>
<ol>
<li>
Right&nbsp;mouse&nbsp;click in the blue AWB Login area</li>
<li>
Select this frame, and Show only this frame</li>
<li>
Right mouse&nbsp;click in the blue AWB Login area</li>
<li>
Select view page information</li>
</ol>
<p>
The page information window will appear confirming the AWB login control is encrypted under SSL connection.</p>
<p>
<img src='/image/1432086655820/firefox-page-info.jpg' alt="Firefox page info" class='    ' title="Firefox page info" />
</p>
<p>
When accessing secure areas of the AWB website, you should use secure passwords that:</p>
<ul>
<li>
cannot be easily guessed</li>
<li>
are not in written form</li>
<li>
are not disclosed to any third party</li>
</ul>
<p>
To ensure your security you should always take your own precautions which includes running reputable anti-virus software on your computer.&nbsp;</p>
<p>
AWB may vary or replace its security policies from time to time.</p>
<p>
If you have any questions about security and this website, please contact the Grower Services Centre on 1800 447 246.</p>
</div>
